WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.201 --> 00:00:11.243
Diego Alvarez: Thanks for jumping on, both. I know this was short notice. Raj, Greg, how's the week going over there?

2
00:00:12.381 --> 00:00:23.037
Greg Hollis: Busy. We're two weeks out from the Q4 push and I've got three rooftops short a BDC rep, so I'm covering some of that myself.

3
00:00:23.418 --> 00:00:31.260
Raj Malhotra: Same here. Month end close is next week and I've got auditors in the building, so I'll keep my part tight.

4
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:39.290
Diego Alvarez: Understood. I put thirty minutes on the invite, and I don't think we'll need all of it.

5
00:00:39.527 --> 00:00:54.336
Raj Malhotra: Good, because I want to talk about money. December's renewal is on the calendar, and I have a competing bid in front of me that comes in noticeably lower per rooftop than what we're paying you.

6
00:00:55.181 --> 00:01:00.387
Diego Alvarez: Okay. Can you tell me who that is and what's in the scope?

7
00:01:01.571 --> 00:01:13.977
Raj Malhotra: Marchex. And the thing that keeps catching my CFO's eye is that their per-rooftop number already includes call scoring, so on paper it's roughly a thirty percent gap at our current rooftop count.

8
00:01:14.321 --> 00:01:18.977
Diego Alvarez: That's a real gap. What's the rooftop count they quoted against, all twenty-two?

9
00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:29.227
Raj Malhotra: All twenty-two, across both states. He had it on one page with no implementation fee attached, which is what made him forward it to me.

10
00:01:29.746 --> 00:01:39.388
Greg Hollis: From my side it's less about the headline number and more that their bundle gives me scoring as a line item I'm already paying for separately today.

11
00:01:40.836 --> 00:01:54.288
Diego Alvarez: Got it. I'm not going to argue pricing on this call, I don't own that. What I'd like is the quote itself so I can bring it into the renewal conversation with the right people internally.

12
00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:59.089
Raj Malhotra: I can forward you the PDF tonight. It's dated last Thursday.

13
00:01:59.347 --> 00:02:06.252
Diego Alvarez: Perfect, send it to my normal address. And remind me, is the scoring they're describing per call or per rooftop?

14
00:02:06.618 --> 00:02:10.515
Raj Malhotra: Per rooftop. That's the whole pitch, one number, everything's inside it.

15
00:02:11.213 --> 00:02:20.521
Greg Hollis: While we're on it, nothing's broken on our end. Call tracking and the signals are doing what we expect. This is a commercial question.

16
00:02:21.154 --> 00:02:24.547
Diego Alvarez: Good to hear. How's volume looking this month?

17
00:02:25.369 --> 00:02:34.938
Greg Hollis: We're tracking around eleven thousand calls for September across the group, up maybe four percent from August. Phoenix and the two Vegas stores are carrying most of that.

18
00:02:35.815 --> 00:02:40.886
Diego Alvarez: And the tax season bump you usually see in February, is that still the plan?

19
00:02:41.376 --> 00:02:47.074
Greg Hollis: Yeah, that's when we lean on it hardest. Our BDC schedules around it.

20
00:02:48.565 --> 00:02:56.397
Diego Alvarez: Okay, I'll make a note. Anything on the scheduling side I should know before we set the next review?

21
00:02:57.014 --> 00:03:06.634
Greg Hollis: Only that Thursdays are bad now, we've got the regional ops call at nine. Tuesday or Wednesday afternoons work better for me.

22
00:03:08.072 --> 00:03:11.811
Diego Alvarez: I'll move it. Let's say the twentieth, two o'clock your time?

23
00:03:13.032 --> 00:03:13.832
Greg Hollis: That works.

24
00:03:14.614 --> 00:03:30.862
Raj Malhotra: Before we wrap, I want to be clear this isn't a threat. I'd rather keep the platform we have. I just can't walk into a renewal with a lower per-rooftop bid in my folder and nothing to say about it.

25
00:03:31.976 --> 00:03:42.574
Diego Alvarez: That's fair, and I'd do the same in your seat. Timing-wise, does your CFO want an answer before the December first date or is that flexible?

26
00:03:43.637 --> 00:03:49.680
Raj Malhotra: He'd like something in writing by mid-November so it can go into the budget cycle.

27
00:03:50.564 --> 00:03:59.409
Diego Alvarez: Mid-November, okay. Let me take that internally, along with the quote, and come back to you with a real answer instead of a maybe.

28
00:04:00.552 --> 00:04:02.219
Raj Malhotra: That's all I'm asking.

29
00:04:03.289 --> 00:04:10.919
Greg Hollis: One small thing, is the reporting you send us monthly going to keep coming through the same way? My team saves those.

30
00:04:11.224 --> 00:04:15.414
Diego Alvarez: Nothing changing there, they'll keep landing the same day each month.

31
00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.240
Greg Hollis: Good.

32
00:04:17.833 --> 00:04:31.879
Diego Alvarez: Alright. Raj, send me the Marchex quote tonight, Greg, I'll move the review to the twentieth at two. I'll follow up by Friday with who I've talked to and what the next step looks like.

33
00:04:33.332 --> 00:04:34.933
Raj Malhotra: Sounds good. Thanks, Diego.

34
00:04:36.307 --> 00:04:37.435
Greg Hollis: Thanks. Talk soon.

35
00:04:38.376 --> 00:04:39.649
Diego Alvarez: Take care, both.
